  "description": "Pakistan - Solar Radiation Measurement Data is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Extractive industries, Solar\", published or maintained by Roman Affolter (World Bank Group). Data repository for measurements from 9 automated solar stations in Pakistan. Data will be uploaded in batches, on a monthly basis, and will transmit daily reports on 10 minute average values for solar radiation levels, temperature, air pressure and wind speed. Coverage: Pakistan. It has 26 files in CSV, ZIP, XLS. The portal files it under Extractive industries, Solar. The portal gives 2016 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. It can support power-system and electrification planning studies. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
